        <div class="re-label">What this job is</div>
        <div class="re-text">Second-in-command — becomes Governor if the Governor can't serve. Also <strong>presides over the PA Senate</strong> (can cast tie-breaking votes) and <strong>chairs the Board of Pardons</strong>, which reviews clemency for people in Pennsylvania prisons.</div>
      </div>
      <div class="re-block">
        <div class="re-label">Real power</div>
        <div class="re-text">Board of Pardons chair — direct power over who gets released or has a record cleared. Senate tie-breaking vote. Emergency management oversight. Full Governor powers if needed.</div>
      </div>
      <div class="re-block">
        <div class="re-label">Why it matters to Philadelphia</div>
        <div class="re-text">Philadelphia has the highest incarceration rate of any large American city. The Lt. Governor chairs the board that reviews every clemency petition in PA. That's significant direct power over Philadelphians inside the state prison system.</div>
      </div>
